  "description": "The existing premises currently operate as a beauty salon (Use Class E). The proposal involves subdividing the internal space to accommodate a secondary use, a café/brunch area, while allowing the beauty salon to continue its operations as usual.\n\nThe internal separation will be achieved by constructing a non-load-bearing plasterboard partition wall, creating two clearly defined but connected commercial units within the same building footprint.\n\nExternally, the proposal includes the addition of one new entrance door on the front elevation. This new door will be installed directly adjacent to the existing salon entrance and will serve as a dedicated entrance for the café. It will match the existing door in size, style, and glazing, ensuring visual continuity and minimal impact on the external appearance of the building.\n\nThe building’s current frontage is primarily glazed, and the installation of the additional door will be carried out within this glazed section. There will be no changes to the building’s footprint, no structural alterations to load-bearing elements, and no impact on the overall structural integrity or appearance of the building. All works are internal and minor in scale, and no external extensions or significant alterations are proposed.\n\n",
